  "title": "Melnikov's valency-variety problem",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Problem The valency-variety $w(G)$ of a graph $G$ is the number of different degrees in $G$. Is the chromatic number of any graph $G$ with at least two vertices greater than $$\\ceil{ \\frac{\\floor{w(G)/2}}{|V(G)| - w(G)} } ~?$$",
